bunsen-configs-wayland-plugin
=============================

This package holds configuration files and scripts to add a Wayland session
to an existing BunsenLabs Carbon system.

The main content is:

*) Configuration for a BunsenLabs Wayland session at startup, triggered
from a desktop file in /usr/share/wayland-sessions.

*) A collection of user configuration files templates,
stored in /usr/share/bunsen/skel. Installation of these user files is
triggered from the Bunsenlabs Wayland session.

*) Dependencies on the necessary, or desirable, additional packages needed,
notably labwc the default wayland compositor.
Others include xwwall gtklock xss-lock grim slurp and tofi.

Most of the utilities currently installed on a BunsenLabs Carbon X11 system
also run on Wayland.
